<para id="RM0000012U100SX" category="C" type-id="303BZ" name-id="065A0-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P0327/52</dtccode>
<dtcname>Knock Sensor Circuit1 (Low)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0328/52</dtccode>
<dtcname>Knock Sensor Circuit1 (High)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000012U100SX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002UB00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The knock control sensor is installed on the cylinder block and detects engine knocking. The knock control sensor contains a sensor that generates voltage when the cylinder block vibrates and deforms due to knocking. When knocking occurs, the engine control computer retards the ignition timing to suppress knocking.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
