<subpara id="RM0000012U100SX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00002UD00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the Freeze Frame Data. Freeze frame data records part of the engine operating condition when a malfunction occurs, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000012U100SX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000012U100SX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00002UE00000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Knock Control Value)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Apply the parking brake and chock the wheels.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Start the engine and warm it up.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Select the data monitor item [Knock Control Value] from [Diagnosis Function Menu] → [ECU Data Monitor].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the change in the data monitor [Knock Control Value] when the engine operating condition is changed.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Measurement Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The monitor display value changes.</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Create driving conditions that change the advance correction control. (Perform a stall test, race the engine, apply the A/C or other electrical loads, etc.)</ptxt>
</atten4>
<atten2>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When performing a stall test, always take measures to prevent the vehicle from moving suddenly, and confirm that there is no one nearby before performing it.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not continue the stall test for 5 seconds or more.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten2>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>Reference Values </title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Monitor Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Normal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Malfunction (DTC detected)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Knock Control Value</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>-3.0 to 2.0°CA</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Does not change</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The above table shows reference values, so the same values may not necessarily be displayed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000012U100SX_04_0010" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000012U100SX_04_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
